{"created": "2026-10-13T04:01:15.568262+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-13T04:01:16.394637+00:00", "id": 23331080, "conceptrecid": "23331079", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23331080", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23331079", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23331080", "metadata": {"title": "Loss of total-space positivity for the normalized relative K\u00e4hler\u2013Ricci flow", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23331080", "publication_date": "2026-10-12", "description": "<p>We give a negative answer to the total-space positivity-preservation question for the probability-normalized relative K\u00e4hler\u2013Ricci flow defined by Naumann on O_E(r). For E = O(1) \u2295 O(1) over the projective line, a smooth strictly positive initial metric on O_E(2) = O(2,2) evolves to horizontal curvature exactly \u22121/96 at time (log 2)/2. The four-page research note proves global initial positivity and derives the exact second-variation evolution along a stationary central fiber.</p><p>The flow construction was already known; the result addresses the explicit positivity question in the original report and published article, rather than the Griffiths conjecture or other normalizations. The deposit includes manuscript source, reproducible exact verification, independent mathematical audits, and a bounded primary-source priority audit. Historical first priority is not asserted; a relevant 2025 Naumann habilitation was identified but its text was not recovered. Smooth finite-time flow existence is a cited analytic input, not a computational conclusion.</p><p>AI tools were used extensively in development, writing, reproduction, and adversarial verification. This is an unrefereed preprint with internal AI adversarial reviews; it has not received human peer review.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kriebel, Alec", "affiliation": "Independent researcher", "orcid": "0009-0001-9320-500X"}], "keywords": ["relative K\u00e4hler\u2013Ricci flow", "total-space positivity", "projective bundles", "positive Hermitian metrics", "Griffiths positivity", "counterexample", "exact symbolic verification"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/521", "relation": "isDerivedFrom", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "10.4310/MRL.2021.v28.n5.a10", "relation": "cites", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.4171/OWR/2017/39", "relation": "cites", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.2140/apde.2013.6.131", "relation": "cites", "scheme": "doi"}], "version": "1.0", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23331079"}}]}}, "title": "Loss of total-space positivity for the normalized relative K\u00e4hler\u2013Ricci flow", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23331080", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23331080", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23331080?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23331080", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23331080", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23331080", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23331080/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23331079", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23331079", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23331079", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23331079", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23331080/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23331080/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23331080/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23331080/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23331080:positivity_loss.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23331080:positivity_loss.pdf/full